---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TileArt from '../../components/TileArt.astro';
---
<Layout
	title="Free logic puzzles to play"
	description="Play Binairo and Star Battle free in your browser. No sign-up, undo and keyboard play built in, and hints that open one layer at a time."
>
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="game-head">
			<h1>Games</h1>
			<p>Each puzzle has a fresh board for today and as many extra boards as you like.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="table-grid">
			<a class="tile" href="/play/binairo/">
				<TileArt kind="binairo" />
				<div>
					<h2>Binairo</h2>
					<p>Fill the grid with suns and moons. No three alike in a row, and every row and column balanced. 6×6, 8×8 and 10×10.</p>
				</div>
			</a>
			<a class="tile" href="/play/sudoku/">
				<TileArt kind="sudoku" />
				<div>
					<h2>Sudoku</h2>
					<p>Classic 9×9 with notes and hints that name the technique. Easy, medium and hard.</p>
				</div>
			</a>
			<a class="tile" href="/play/star-battle/">
				<TileArt kind="star" />
				<div>
					<h2>Star Battle</h2>
					<p>One star in every row, column and region. Stars may not touch, even at a corner. Boards from 6×6 to 9×9.</p>
				</div>
			</a>
			<a class="tile" href="/play/word-box/">
				<TileArt kind="wordbox" />
				<div>
					<h2>Word box solver</h2>
					<p>Type the twelve letters of a four-sided word box and open the hints one layer at a time. A helper rather than a daily game.</p>
				</div>
			</a>
		</div>
		<div class="section-head">
			<h2>More on the way</h2>
			<p class="lede">Killer Sudoku, KenKen and Hitori are next. They will appear here once each one plays well on a phone.</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
